{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"x69z","tool":"context.node_rule","arguments":{"mode":"compact"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"actor_role\": \"PI\", \"errors\": [], \"ok\": true, \"result\": {\"context\": \"Auto-research recording contract\\nTemplate-driven node recording:\\n- Use node.add as the single PI-facing node creation tool.\\n- parents=[] creates a root; one parent creates a child; two or more parents create a merge.\\nNode edit and review rules:\\n- Use node.edit for human review, PI conclusions, questions, status corrections, and effective field edits.\\n- Use node.edit.resolves to close PI Inbox items. Mentioning a ref in free text is only evidence and does not close the reminder.\\n- Use new_status for node lifecycle changes; do not patch status as a regular field.\\nNode removal rules:\\n- Use node.remove for effective-view deletion; raw nodes.jsonl and edges.jsonl are not physically rewritten.\\n- mode=hide hides one node from default views without changing lineage.\\n- mode=detach removes one effective edge. If it would orphan a child, provide replacement_parent_id or promote_children_to_roots=true.\\n- mode=prune removes a node from the effective view. Non-leaf prune requires cascade=true with cascade_confirmed=true, replacement_parent_id, or promote_children_to_roots=true.\", \"mode\": \"compact\"}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
